# T-052 — build context for both back-end/Dockerfile and front-end/Dockerfile (context: portal/,
# see docker-compose.yml). Keeps the context small and, more importantly, keeps stray
# uncommitted artefacts from a working tree (a scratch file, a local `dist/`) out of a
# reproducible image build — `tsc`'s inferred `rootDir` is sensitive to exactly this kind of
# stray file at a workspace root (an uncommitted `tmp-*` script sitting next to `src/` widens
# `rootDir` to include it, and the build output nests under `dist/src/...` instead of
# `dist/...` for everyone, not just the image build). None of this is git-related the way the
# root `.gitignore` is; a Docker build has no `.git` in scope by default and does not read it.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
**/.turbo
.git
.github

# Local env files — never baked into an image (R4). docker-compose.yml supplies configuration
# via its own `environment`/`env_file`, never a file copied into the build context.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor/OS noise
.DS_Store
*.log

# Uncommitted scratch files some agents' verification sessions leave at a workspace root
# (e.g. `back-end/tmp-*`) — never intended to ship, and never intended to be a build input.
**/tmp-*

# Not needed inside either image — both Dockerfiles copy only the package.json + src they need.
**/*.md
front-end/coverage
front-end/.storybook
front-end/storybook-static
e2e
